# Review: NativePlugin

The three native features exist: the spotlight listener, the OTA updater and the Ollama sidecar all live in
`src/capabilities/` and do roughly what the spec says. Nothing in the package is tested — there is no test
file or story in `plugin-native` — so every implemented item is `untested` and every scenario is `missing`.

The update types moved to `@dxos/app-toolkit/AppUpdate` (shared with plugin-pwa) and grew a `dev` status,
which is the biggest divergence: a dev-server build on a supported platform reports `dev`, not
`unsupported` (UpdateStatus, F-2.4, T-5). The three "ops" are methods on the `UpdateManager` capability, not
operations. The Ollama sidecar activates on `ActivationEvents.Startup` and spawns lazily on first use, not on
`AssistantEvents.SetupAiServiceProviders` (F-3.1).

Of 26 items: 0 done, 16 untested, 1 partial, 3 diverged, 6 missing.

